# A user-written accumulator: a Fold that builds a Map one insert at a time,
# reading it in the same expression that writes it. Every update is
# semantically functional; the optimizer's linear-accumulator pass proves the
# copied-from value is dead and lets both backends write through instead.
#
# Without that pass this is quadratic in the map, not linear in the writes —
# which is the difference between a benchmark and an unusable program.
Cursed Energy: stdin
Cursed Technique: Split Text by "\n"
Channeled Energy: Convert List to Integers
Maximum Technique: Fold
    Seed: (xs) -> emptymap(0, 0)
    Using: (acc, x) -> insert(acc, x % 50000, getor(acc, x % 50000, 0) + 1)
Cursed Technique: Apply
    Using: (m) -> size(m) + max(values(m))
Reveal: stdout
